//
// Probe: Q18. Can a word observe `q` at a value other than 100.0?
//
// Two RFC-0001 drafts rendered `q` as the constant 100.0. It is a field, not
// a constant — but no word writes it. Arithmetic does not average it: `+`
// calls `numeric_op` directly and never reaches `calc_q`, which has no caller
// (Q35; D32 as amended 2026-09-10). Constructors start at 100.0, and
// `Value::none` starts at 0.0 instead
// (create_special.rs:19-21, value.rs:38), and `json.to_value` returns it for
// a JSON null (cast_json_to_value.rs:39).
//
// Both words are registered and in scope, so the path is reachable.
//
"probe: json null converts to a value carrying q 0.0, not 100.0" println
"null" json json.to_value
debug.display_stack

"probe: for contrast, an ordinary integer sits at the 100.0 fixpoint" println
42
debug.display_stack
